            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="0305" n="1355" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">357.AB/3–3054: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-03-30T16:00:00-05:00">March 30, 1954—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>548. Re Kashmir observers. Re urtel 448, March
                    29, after delivery of <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> I conveyed to
                        Hammarskjold the gist of your paragraph 2. He expressed
                    complete understanding of our position and said he would be glad to have us
                    advise the Indians, that while we recognize that it is up to the Secretary
                    General to make a decision, that we have no national interest in maintaining our
                    observers in Kashmir. He gave me copies of his letter to Dayal on clarification status observers and
                    consultations on replacement of observers and of his new instructions to Nimmo
                    on direction and discipline of observers. (Copies being pouched tonight.)</p>
                <p>In view of big point which Menon made of
                    this in several different conversations with me, it would be helpful to my
                    future relations with him here if I could advise him myself of US position.</p>
                <p>Request, therefore, that Ambassador Allen
                    convey the message to Menon on my
                    behalf. We are advising Dayal here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
